composio-bridge — third-party attribution
=========================================

This component adapts the Composio connection pattern pioneered by OpenMausBot:

    OpenMausBot — https://github.com/milind-soni/OpenMausBot
    Copyright the OpenMausBot contributors
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Specifically, the following designs and API-call sequences in
`composio.ts` and `state.ts` are adapted from OpenMausBot's
`server/composio-session.ts` and `server/composio-project.ts`:

  * using a Composio *project* API key (ak_…) with the `x-api-key` header
    against https://backend.composio.dev/api/v3.1 (no SDK);
  * one reusable Tool Router Session per stable user id, with
    multi-account mode and explicit account selection;
  * per-toolkit discovery of the project's own auth configs, and turning
    on Tool Router for them via PATCH /auth_configs/{id};
  * `revoke_on_delete=true` on disconnect.

The code here is rewritten for Pantheon's Node sidecar and is not a verbatim
copy; the behaviour is intentionally kept compatible.

